<div id=3D"text-3f63814ee0" class=3D"cmp-text">
    <h2>NYCU Modernizes IC Design Education with AMD EPYC=E2=84=A2 Server C=
PUs</h2>
<p><span class=3D"subheadline">NYCU scaled its IC design training to suppor=
t 500 concurrent users by deploying a secure private cloud powered by 4th G=
en AMD EPYC Server CPUs</span></p>

</div>

   =20


</div>
<div class=3D"text aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12">

<div id=3D"text-b1db1a2d5e" class=3D"cmp-text">
    <p>As semiconductor manufacturing moves to more advanced process techno=
logies, the compute and simulation demands of IC design and Electronic Desi=
gn Automation (EDA) workloads continue to rise. Yet many university teachin=
g environments have remained focused on legacy planar nodes, creating a dis=
connect between academia and industry. With support from Taiwan=E2=80=99s M=
inistry of Education Talent Cultivation Project for Advanced IC Design, Nat=
ional Yang Ming Chiao Tung University (NYCU) deployed a secure private clou=
d environment powered by 4th Gen AMD EPYC=E2=84=A2 Server CPUs to bring adv=
anced process IC design workflows into the classroom and research lab.</p>

</div>

   =20


</div>
<div class=3D"pullquote aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12"><aside =
data-cmp-is=3D"pullquote" class=3D"pullquote">
    <figure>NYCU needed an isolated, self-managed infrastructure that could=
 provide both the performance and security required for industry-relevant I=
C design education.</figure>
    <figcaption>Professor Ming-Dou Ker, Associate Dean of the College of El=
ectrical and Computer Engineering at NYCU</figcaption>
</aside>

   =20

</div>
<div class=3D"text aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12">

<div id=3D"text-ecd77e0499" class=3D"cmp-text">
    <p>According to Professor Ming-Dou Ker, Associate Dean of the College o=
f Electrical and Computer Engineering at NYCU, the university=E2=80=99s pre=
vious course environments relied on standard PCs for remote access. Under h=
eavy workloads such as large-scale Monte Carlo analysis and auto placement =
and routing (APR), performance became a bottleneck. Post-layout simulations=
 could take up to a week per run, slowing down iterative design and validat=
ion and limiting the effectiveness of instruction.</p>
<p>As FinFET-based design was introduced into coursework, the challenge ext=
ended beyond compute performance. Advanced-node process parameters, design =
rules, and PDK data require strict protection, making public cloud deployme=
nt less viable. NYCU needed an isolated, self-managed infrastructure that c=
ould provide both the performance and security required for industry-releva=
nt IC design education.</p>

</div>

   =20


</div>
<div class=3D"image aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12">






















<div id=3D"image-40a0f87374" class=3D"cmp-image" itemtype=3D"http://schema.=
org/ImageObject" itemscope=3D"">

=09
=09

=09
=09
=09
=09
=09




